The source code of PDF-Knead is available to read, but PDF-Knead is not open-source software: commercial use of the paid features
and any commercial distribution require a license from the Licensor.


1 Definitions

(1) “Software”: the program PDF-Knead in executable form and as source code together with the files of its project, without the
    components of other projects (section 9).
(2) “Results”: files and printouts created or edited with the Software.
(3) “Commercial use”: any use by or for companies, self-employed persons and freelancers in the course of their work, authorities
    and other public administration bodies, and associations that have full-time employees or run a business – including use by
    their employees, members or agents.
(4) “Non-commercial use”: use by private individuals for private purposes, by associations without full-time employees and without
    a business, by schools and universities, and by non-profit organizations.
(5) “Free features”: viewing, searching, printing, the image information, and filling in existing form fields and saving the
    filled-in form. All other features are “paid features”; the Software marks them.
(6) “Commercial distribution”: any distribution or provision of the Software that earns money – in particular against payment, as
    part of a paid product or offer, through download offers financed by fees or advertising, or as a service for others (for
    example over the internet) for which payment is charged.


2 Use without a license fee

(1) For non-commercial use, the Software may be used with all features without a license fee.
(2) For commercial use, the free features may be used without a license fee.


3 Commercial use of the paid features

(1) Commercial use of the paid features requires a commercial license, granted by the Licensor in a separate contract. Scope, term
    and price follow from that contract.
(2) For evaluation, the paid features may be used commercially for 30 days from first use without a commercial license.
(3) License keys must not be passed on to third parties outside the licensee.


4 Results

The Results belong to the user. This license does not restrict their use; they may also be sold. Rights of third parties in the
processed content remain unaffected.


5 Distribution of the Software

(1) The unmodified Software may be distributed as long as no money is earned with it. It must be distributed complete, together
    with this license, the file THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and the license texts of the components of other projects.
(2) Any commercial distribution is not permitted. The Licensor reserves the distribution of the Software.


6 Modifications

(1) The Software may be modified for one's own use.
(2) Modified versions of the Software must not be distributed or made available to others.
(3) The license check, the registration, the marking of the paid features, and license and copyright notices must not be removed,
    altered or circumvented – not even in a version for one's own use.


7 Use of parts of the code

(1) Individual parts of the source code may be used in one's own private, non-commercial projects. Using the Software as a whole or
    substantial parts of it is not permitted.
(2) Such projects may be published as long as no money is earned with them.
(3) Every such use must name PDF-Knead as the source, with a reference to this license. The parts taken over remain under this
